  "step_2": "The individual considered the monetary difference of 100 Euros between the possible winnings (2500 vs. 2400) and compared it to the difference in probabilities (34% vs. 33%). The individual notes that the higher reward (2500 Euros) was only 1% less likely (33% vs. 34%), and therefore justified choosing the higher reward despite the slightly higher risk. The deliberation focuses on the trade-off between a small decrease in probability (1%) and a significant increase in potential gain (100 Euros). The individual’s justification centers on the favorable risk-reward ratio, not on the distribution of probability mass relative to favorable outcomes.",
